==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|avec|lang=frm}}, {{term|avecques||with|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|avoc|lang=fro}}, {{term|avoec|lang=fro}}, {{term|avuec||with|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{term|abhoc|aboc, abhoc|lang=la}}, a {{frk}} corruption of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{term|apud hoc||with this, near this, close to this|lang=la}}.  Used as a replacement of {{la}} {{term|cum||with|lang=la}} in [[w:Merovingian|Merovingian]] and [[w:Carolingian|Carolingian]] documents. Gradually supplanted Old French {{term|od||with|lang=fro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-avec.ogg|audio}}
